# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Binary assets: never line-ending-converted.
# The generated fixtures contain no NUL byte, so git's auto-detection classifies
# them as text and a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites their LFs to
# CRLF -- which corrupts bytes that test_fixtures.py asserts by SHA-256.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary

# Modèles Tesseract : binaires, et vérifiés par SHA-256 (voir _tessdata/SHA256SUMS).
# Une conversion de fin de ligne les corromprait en silence.
*.traineddata binary
